{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The first fruits of the wheat harvest.</b> For on it you bring the two loaves from the wheat." "<b>First fruits.</b> For it is the first meal-offering brought from the new grain of wheat to the Sanctuary — since the meal-offering of the omer brought on Pesach is from barley (Menachot 4)." "<b>And the festival of ingathering.</b> At the time when you gather your produce from the field into the house; אֲסִיפָה here is a term of bringing into the house, as in ״וְאָסַפְתּוֹ אֶל תּוֹךְ בֵּיתֶךָ״ (Deuteronomy 22)." "<b>The turn of the year.</b> For it is at the return of the year — at the beginning of the coming year." "<b>Turn.</b> A term of cycle and circuit."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:34.065742282Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}